screens.prose:
This is **divide and conquer**: split the problem, solve each half the same way, combine the answers. With indices, `max_rec(xs, lo, hi)` looks at `xs[lo]` to `xs[hi]`.

```python
def max_rec(xs, lo, hi):
    if lo == hi:
        return xs[lo]
    mid = (lo + hi) // 2
    left = max_rec(xs, lo, mid)
    right = max_rec(xs, mid + 1, hi)
    return max(left, right)
```

